    "setupNotes": [
      "Official 2.1.24 Space Age; one chemical plant (solid fuel from light oil) and two assembling machine 2 (rocket fuel), no modules, red belts, fast inserters, one medium electric pole (no substation). WEST: light oil 660/min into the west pipe; it feeds all three machines. EAST: one red belt exit on the bottom row, 6 rocket fuel/min, one machine per lane. Solid fuel is handed machine to machine. The two solid-fuel arms are wired to the exit belt tile and run only while it holds fewer than 8 rocket fuel, so the machines stop soon after the consumer stops taking fuel and restart by themselves; keep that red wire and condition. Supply electricity at the medium pole.",
      "Place this supplier west of rocket supplies with its exit row (row 6 from its top) on the rocket-fuel entrance row and join them with a straight red belt. One copy covers rocket supplies (it takes about 5 rocket fuel a minute).",
